N5008 [temp.spec.partial.order]/1: libstdc++'s extent_v has both
`extent_v<_Tp[_Size], 0>` and `extent_v<_Tp[_Size], _Uint>`; for
`extent_v<int[5]>` both match and the former is more specialised.  The
variable-template instantiation used to take the LAST match in scope order,
yielding 0 (and ranges::size(array) returned 0).  Ordered by deduction as the
class-template case already was.  Non-vacuous: the last assertion states a
wrong value and must FAIL.
